{
 "about": "Same-game correlation table, Chat 8 Phase 3 (docs/correlation.md). rho is the correlation of two legs' latent normals, each oriented so higher = the YES of an over / a win; a NO leg flips the sign. Frozen by its sha256 (CRLF normalized to LF); Phase 4's pre-registration names the hash. workers/consensus/correlation_rho.json is a byte-identical copy (tests/test_correlation.py).",
 "version": "2026-11-11.4",
 "keys": "self|a|b one player's two kinds; mate|a|b teammates; opp|a|b opponents (a <= b); team|<kind>|<line> a player with his own club's win or cover, or the game total (over); a player with the OTHER club's line takes the team row with its sign flipped where the league has no draw (owner, Nov 11: no opponent rows), else unmodeled; game|<a>|<b> two game lines (a club line with the other club's: the sign flips where there is no draw).",
